      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/oakville_connecticut",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1852, the Oakville Company launched garment hardware production, drawing Irish and Italian workers to the Naugatuck Valley’s brass mills.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/oakville_connecticut",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Oakville Museum at Bronte Creek preserves artifacts that tell stories of early settlers and their daily lives.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
